From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 21:38:02 -0400
Subject: round: a folder close is one Recently Closed entry, the lit chip,
 quiet starts
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The Mac's round of 2026-10-12 and 13 on the operator's word, as one
patch: its fixups would conflict with the archive and test layouts that
patches 0058 to 0061 changed.

A folder close as one entry (PLAN.md TAB-13, folders F19): Close Folder's
Tabs marks each tab with the close's batch and the folder's name. The app
menu's Recently Closed and the Mac's History menu show a batch as one
folder item; Restore Folder and ⇧⌘T bring the whole folder back. The list
keeps an entry per tab, so Undo and the Archived view are unchanged.

The lit chip (PLAN.md SPC-4, spaces B12): the chip under dragged rows that
it would take is lit in its Space's colour.

The extension-reload test (PLAN.md CMD-1, F61): an extension reloaded and
disabled under the open command bar leaves it whole.

Quiet starts (privacy Q11 to Q13): the browser tests of the code in patch
0030, no push service and no Google account check at start, and the
Security page's word on Safe Browsing.

A dangling pointer the Mac's checked build found: the tab layout's
animation maps kept rows that were destroyed outright (a folder closed, a
window restored). The layout manager forgets a child when its host loses
it.

Split panes are the page (splits J7): no padding inside a pane, so both
pages start right under the address row, keep the card's gutters and lie
a card gutter apart.

The row off the traffic lights (sidebar Y19): while the strip is narrower
than the rail, as when a hidden sidebar opens, the row's contents start
past the lights.

A private window's row in the page's colour (private V9, half of PLAN.md
WIN-6): a private or Guest window owns its page colour, and a private
window's row supplier stands for the private mark in its colour key.

Why: the operator asked for the Phase 0 items with code left and the two
privacy leaks at startup, tested properly, and then reported the split
view's gaps, the traffic lights on Back in a test window, and Back,
Forward and Reload with no ground under them; each change has its
behaviour id and tests that failed before the fix.
Removable when: never; these are Stedding's own behaviours.
